00:21:55.213 --> 00:21:56.882
simply for doing their job.

00:21:56.882 --> 00:21:59.384
We got to defend brave journalists

00:21:59.384 --> 00:22:01.953
most national stories in this country

00:22:02.254 --> 00:22:05.223
at some point were first a local story

00:22:08.727 --> 00:22:09.428
and

00:22:13.265 --> 00:22:13.965
those stories

00:22:13.965 --> 00:22:16.001
and championed by reporters at outlets

00:22:16.001 --> 00:22:17.703
that many of them have now folded.

00:22:17.703 --> 00:22:18.670
If we can't figure out a way

00:22:18.670 --> 00:22:19.671
to pay local reporters,

00:22:19.671 --> 00:22:20.639
then as a country

00:22:20.639 --> 00:22:21.840
we're only left with that

00:22:21.840 --> 00:22:23.008
many more blind spots

00:22:23.008 --> 00:22:25.444
to where the ball is happening.

00:22:30.148 --> 00:22:31.850
You hear about all these newsrooms

00:22:31.850 --> 00:22:32.684
getting cut, says

00:22:32.684 --> 00:22:33.452
every article

00:22:33.452 --> 00:22:34.152
that Tamra's

00:22:34.152 --> 00:22:34.886
been sending me in

00:22:34.886 --> 00:22:36.154
the last two months is just

00:22:36.154 --> 00:22:38.223
the newsroom is getting cut, cut.

00:22:38.223 --> 00:22:38.857
And people

00:22:38.857 --> 00:22:39.825
were cutting budgets,

00:22:39.825 --> 00:22:41.560
but you never hear about the multimillion

00:22:41.560 --> 00:22:42.494
dollar executives

00:22:42.494 --> 00:22:43.562
reducing their salaries

00:22:43.562 --> 00:22:45.964
within these organizations.

00:22:50.102 --> 00:22:52.771
Now, how do we fix this

00:22:53.672 --> 00:22:54.139
I don't know.

00:22:54.139 --> 00:22:54.840
I'm a comedian.

00:22:54.840 --> 00:22:56.308
I was just up in

00:22:57.609 --> 00:22:59.244
It's not my job to have the solution

00:22:59.244 --> 00:23:00.312
that's we got.

00:23:01.646 --> 00:23:04.049
But local local reporting

00:23:04.049 --> 00:23:05.484
is very important.

00:23:05.650 --> 00:23:07.252
My mother is here tonight

00:23:08.720 --> 00:23:09.721
and

00:23:12.824 --> 00:23:14.526
I know she's furious right now

00:23:14.526 --> 00:23:15.660
because I'm trying to put on camera.

00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:17.462
But my mother was among

00:23:17.462 --> 00:23:19.131
a group of black student protesters

00:23:19.131 --> 00:23:20.732
fighting for equality in the sixties.

00:23:20.732 --> 00:23:23.668
At Delta State University and

00:23:25.337 --> 00:23:26.104
and

00:23:26.838 --> 00:23:29.107
that was a dangerous time.

00:23:29.107 --> 00:23:30.475
But those types of incidents

00:23:30.475 --> 00:23:32.010
were covered by local reporters.

00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:32.944
And some of the shame

00:23:32.944 --> 00:23:33.412
that came

00:23:33.412 --> 00:23:34.846
from the national embarrassment

00:23:34.846 --> 00:23:37.015
of treating people inhumanely.

00:23:37.015 --> 00:23:38.150
It's part of the pressure

00:23:38.150 --> 00:23:39.017
that helped to create

00:23:39.017 --> 00:23:40.652
that type of change.

00:23:40.652 --> 00:23:41.853
What would have become of my mother

00:23:41.853 --> 00:23:42.821
and those of the protesters

00:23:42.821 --> 00:23:43.622
of a local journalist

00:23:43.622 --> 00:23:45.991
wasn't there telling the story

00:23:48.593 --> 00:23:50.996
and now is no different.

00:23:50.996 --> 00:23:51.563
But thankfully,

00:23:51.563 --> 00:23:53.465
my mother's story was told

00:23:53.465 --> 00:23:54.566
she got to complete a degree

00:23:54.566 --> 00:23:55.200
at Delta State

00:23:55.200 --> 00:23:56.401
and continued on the Florida

00:23:56.401 --> 00:23:57.936
A&amp;M and got another degree.

00:23:57.936 --> 00:23:59.838
And then for the last 45 years

00:23:59.838 --> 00:24:00.172
has worked

00:24:00.172 --> 00:24:01.106
at a historically black

00:24:01.106 --> 00:24:02.340
colleges and educator

00:24:02.340 --> 00:24:04.242
and administrator and

00:24:10.081 --> 00:24:11.583
one of those many black colleges.

00:24:11.583 --> 00:24:12.617
They need a little bit more funding.

00:24:12.617 --> 00:24:13.952
You've got a 20 on your job

00:24:13.952 --> 00:24:15.854
here to send that down

00:24:15.854 --> 00:24:18.223
to one of the black colleges

00:24:18.256 --> 00:24:20.192
to my mom I say thank you

00:24:20.192 --> 00:24:23.061
for everything you've done for me

00:24:23.061 --> 00:24:26.064
and for helping countless student

00:24:27.232 --> 00:24:29.701
in Birmingham have the opportunity

00:24:29.701 --> 00:24:32.270
to see a college degree

00:24:32.838 --> 00:24:34.706
and to see an opportunity to grow.

00:24:34.706 --> 00:24:35.540
You know,

00:24:46.985 --> 00:24:48.487
my mother's journey

00:24:48.487 --> 00:24:49.688
may not have even begun

00:24:49.688 --> 00:24:51.256
if not for brave journalists

00:24:51.256 --> 00:24:53.158
who chose to chronicle

00:24:53.158 --> 00:24:55.060
history in real time.

00:24:55.060 --> 00:24:57.596
And I don't know how to ever repay my mom

00:24:57.596 --> 00:24:59.698
for what she's done for me

00:24:59.698 --> 00:25:01.199
and what she's done for so many people.

00:25:01.199 --> 00:25:02.434
In Alabama.

00:25:02.434 --> 00:25:04.402
But just know, Mama, if

00:25:04.402 --> 00:25:05.737
if a white billionaire call

00:25:05.737 --> 00:25:06.471
you an offer to buy

00:25:06.471 --> 00:25:07.772
your house, please sell it

00:25:10.442 --> 00:25:12.310
because I might want to become an NFT.

00:25:12.310 --> 00:25:14.179
Thank you so much.

00:25:14.179 --> 00:25:16.481
So the Correspondents Association,

00:25:16.481 --> 00:25:18.250
thank you so much for Tamara Keith.

00:25:18.250 --> 00:25:19.351
Thank you all so much. Good night.

